# ============================================================
#  Character events — Kael, Bram, faculty and staff.
#  (Kael's main arc lives in chain_hollowstar.grim.)
# ============================================================

# ================= KAEL DUMONT =================

@event kael_snowball
title: Snow in Thawmoon
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: rel(kael) >= 10 and month >= 5 and month <= 7
weight: 10
art: snow
tags: social
scene: A courtyard where it is snowing in one small circle only, a boy in a fur coat standing at its centre holding a perfect snowball.
text: It's snowing in the courtyard. Only in a small circle, around Kael, who is holding a snowball and looking at it as though he's never been allowed to throw one.
> left: Leave him to it
  say: When you pass again, the circle of snow is gone, and there's a small, lopsided snowman in its place.
> right: Throw the first one
  rel kael +8
  mood +6
  vigor +1
  say: Your snowball hits him in the ear. He stares. Then he laughs — a real laugh, startled out of him — and the snow triples.

@event kael_cold_hands
title: Cold Hands
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: rel(kael) >= 20 and love(kael) < 35
weight: 10
art: heart
tags: social romance
scene: Two students sitting close in a library alcove, one holding the other's frost-white hand between both of theirs.
text: Kael's hands are always cold. In the library tonight they're so cold the ink in his pen has frozen. He's trying to thaw it with his breath, embarrassed.
> left: Lend him your gloves
  rel kael +5
  say: He wears them for the rest of the term. They're far too small. He doesn't care.
> right: Warm his hands in yours
  rel kael +6
  love kael +6
  say: He goes very still. Then, slowly, the frost on his fingertips melts. "Nobody's ever been warm enough," he says quietly. "Before."

@event kael_confession
title: Thaw
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: love(kael) >= 35 and rel(kael) >= 25 and bond(kael) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: snow
tags: romance
scene: Frost-ferns spreading across a dark window behind a pale boy who is, for once, looking directly at someone.
text: "I was taught not to want things," Kael says. "Wanting things is how they control you." Frost blooms across the window behind him. "I want you. I'm sorry. I don't know what to do with it."
> left: Gently say no
  love kael -20
  rel kael +2
  say: He nods, as if he expected it. "Thank you for being honest. Nobody is." The frost on the window fades slowly.
> right: Show him what to do with it
  bond kael partner
  love kael +15
  mood +10
  say: You kiss him. Every window in the corridor frosts over at once, and then, very slowly, melts.

# ================= BRAM HOLLIS =================

@event bram_intro
title: Running in the Halls
actor: bram
when: not met(bram) and turn >= 2
weight: 12
art: scroll
tags: rival
scene: A burly prefect with a red sash blocking a corridor, a demerit ledger open in one hand and a quill poised.
text: "Running in the halls." A burly prefect with a red sash steps into your path, ledger already open. "Name?" You weren't running. You were walking briskly.
> left: Accept the demerit
  meet bram
  mood -2
  grades -1
  say: He writes your name very slowly, enjoying it. Bram Hollis. You will learn to recognise his footsteps.
> right: Argue
  meet bram
  rel bram -6
  renown +2
  say: "Walking briskly," you insist. Two demerits: one for running, one for "lip". Some students nearby clap quietly.
  grades -2

@event bram_hall_tax
title: The Hall Tax
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: rel(bram) < 10
weight: 12
art: coin
tags: rival money
scene: A prefect leaning against a stone archway, palm out, a line of nervous first-years shuffling past him.
text: Bram has invented a "hall tax" for using the east staircase. Ten crowns. "Maintenance," he says. The first-years are paying. He looks at you expectantly.
> left: Pay it
  gold -10
  rel bram +3
  mood -3
  say: He pockets the coins. "Pleasure." You take the west staircase forever after.
> right: Refuse loudly
  rel bram -8
  renown +3
  chance 50:
    gain watched
    say: The first-years stop paying too. Bram is furious. He'll find a way to make you pay later. He always does.
  else:
    say: Your refusal spreads. Within a week, nobody pays the hall tax. Bram drops it, scowling.

@event bram_sabotage
title: Missing Notes
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: rel(bram) <= -20 and (month == 3 or month == 4 or month == 9 or month == 10)
weight: 14
art: scroll
tags: rival study
scene: An empty desk drawer, a few scattered pages on the floor, a red prefect's sash glimpsed disappearing around a corner.
text: Two days before exams, your revision notes vanish from your desk. All of them. You saw a red sash in the corridor.
> left: Rewrite them from memory (Lore)
  check lore 18:
    lore +2
    say: You rewrite everything in one furious night. Your new notes are better than the old ones. Take that, Bram.
  else:
    grades -5
    health -3
    say: You rewrite what you can. It isn't enough. Exams go worse than they should.
> right: Search his room (Guile)
  check guile 18:
    rel bram -6
    renown +2
    say: You find your notes under his mattress, and also a teddy bear. You take both. You return the bear. Eventually.
  else:
    gain detention
    rel bram -4
    say: He catches you in his room. That's two weeks of detention, and he gets to supervise.

@event bram_crying
title: Behind the Stables
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: met(bram) and turn >= 8 and not flag(bram_softened)
weight: 8
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A big prefect sitting on an upturned bucket behind the stables, a crumpled letter in his fist, shoulders shaking.
text: Behind the stables, you find Bram Hollis sitting on a bucket, crying into a crumpled letter. He sees you and freezes. "If you tell anyone," he begins, but his voice cracks.
> left: Walk away and never mention it
  rel bram +6
  say: You leave. You never tell anyone. Somehow, he knows you didn't. His demerits become fewer.
> right: Sit down and ask what happened
  flag bram_softened
  rel bram +20
  say: His father. A letter saying he's a disappointment, again. "He was a prefect too," Bram says. "Head boy. I'm just... loud." He wipes his face. "Don't be nice to me. I don't know what to do with it."

@event bram_turns
title: An Unexpected Ally
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: flag(bram_softened) and rel(bram) >= 10 and bond(bram) != "friend"
weight: 12
art: shield
tags: social
scene: A prefect stepping between a cornered student and a pair of older bullies, arms crossed.
text: Two sixth-years corner you by the boathouse, looking for trouble. Then a red sash steps between you. "Problem?" says Bram, cracking his knuckles. They leave fast.
> left: Thank him awkwardly
  rel bram +6
  say: "Don't make it weird," he says, and walks off. He's smiling, slightly.
> right: Offer your hand
  rel bram +10
  bond bram friend
  say: He stares at your hand. Then he shakes it, hard. "Fine. Friends. But I'm still giving you demerits." He does. Fewer.

@event bram_duel
title: A Formal Challenge
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: bond(bram) == "rival" or bond(bram) == "nemesis"
weight: 12
art: duel
tags: rival danger
scene: A white glove lying on a dormitory floor, a red sash folded beside it, a crowd peering through the doorway.
text: Bram throws a glove at your feet in front of half the dormitory. "Formal challenge. Dawn. Dueling green. Unless you're a coward." Everyone is watching.
> left: Decline
  renown -4
  mood -3
  say: "Coward," he says, delighted. It sticks for a while. Then people forget. Mostly.
> right: Accept
  check arcana 20 + year * 4:
    renown +8
    rel bram +5
    say: You disarm him in three moves. The crowd goes wild. Bram, on the grass, starts laughing. "Fine," he says. "Fine."
  else:
    health -10
    renown +2
    say: He wins. But it takes him a full ten minutes, and he's limping too. He nods to you after. Grudging respect.

# ================= PROFESSOR THORNE =================

@event thorne_intro
title: The First Question
actor: thorne
when: not met(thorne) and turn >= 1
weight: 16
art: wand
tags: study
scene: A steep lecture theatre, a stern grey-bearded professor pointing a long finger at one student in the middle row.
text: First Arcana lecture. Professor Thorne surveys the room like a hawk over a field of mice. His finger lands on you. "You. What is the first law of the Arcane?"
> left: Admit you don't know
  meet thorne
  rel thorne +4
  say: "Correct answer," he says. "The first law is: know what you don't know. The rest of you, write that down."
> right: Take a guess (Lore)
  meet thorne
  check lore 10:
    rel thorne +5
    grades +2
    say: "Energy follows intention." His eyebrows twitch. "Acceptable." The room exhales.
  else:
    rel thorne -2
    mood -2
    say: Your guess is so wrong the student next to you gasps. Thorne simply says, "No," and moves on.

@event thorne_office_hours
title: Office Hours
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 10 and arcana >= 14
weight: 10
art: candle
tags: study
scene: A cramped office full of scorched books and a single lit candle, a stern professor leaning back in his chair, fingers steepled.
text: Thorne stops you after class. "Your casting is sloppy and your instincts are good. That's an annoying combination. Thursdays. Seven o'clock. My office. Don't be late."
> left: Politely decline — you're stretched thin
  rel thorne -3
  say: "Hm." He seems neither surprised nor pleased. Thorne is rarely either.
> right: Be there at seven
  arcana +3
  rel thorne +8
  health -2
  say: Two hours of brutal drills. At the end, he hands you a book from his own shelf. "Read it. Return it unburnt."

@event thorne_storm_story
title: The Storm Duel
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 20
weight: 8
art: bolt
tags: study
scene: An old professor standing at a rain-lashed window, lightning illuminating a long scar along his jaw.
text: During a thunderstorm, Thorne stops mid-lecture and watches the lightning. "They say I out-dueled a storm once," he says, to nobody in particular. "Would you like to know what actually happened?"
> left: "Yes, sir."
  gain inspired
  rel thorne +5
  say: He lost, he says. Badly. He spent a year learning why. "Losing well," he says, "is the only thing worth teaching." The class is silent.
> right: Stay quiet
  rel thorne +1
  say: He shakes his head and returns to the lecture. You'll always wonder.

@event thorne_recommendation
title: A Letter of Recommendation
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 30 and year == 3
weight: 16
art: letter
tags: study
scene: A wax-sealed envelope on a professor's desk with a student's name written on it in sharp, angular handwriting.
text: Thorne calls you to his office and slides an envelope across the desk. "The Conclave asked for my recommendations. I wrote one. I don't write many." He pauses. "Don't make me regret it."
> left: Thank him sincerely
  flag thorne_letter
  grades +5
  rel thorne +5
  mood +8
  say: "Go away," he says gruffly. "I have marking." You see him smile at the window as you leave.
> right: Ask why you
  flag thorne_letter
  grades +5
  rel thorne +3
  say: "Because you ask questions like that," he says. "Most students don't. Go."

@event thorne_disappointed
title: A Word in Private
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: grades < 30
weight: 14
art: scales
tags: study crisis
scene: A professor standing by his desk with a sheaf of red-marked papers, a student standing awkwardly before him.
text: Thorne holds up your last three essays. All red. "You're better than this," he says. "That's not a compliment. It's an accusation."
> left: Make excuses
  rel thorne -4
  mood -3
  say: He listens to them all and says nothing. The silence is the worst grade yet.
> right: Ask for help
  rel thorne +6
  grades +5
  lore +1
  say: He sighs and pulls out a chair. "Sit. We'll start with the first essay, and we'll stay until it's right."

# ================= OLD MAUD =================

@event maud_chickens
title: The Great Chicken Escape
actor: maud
when: not met(maud) and turn >= 2
weight: 12
art: feather
tags: nature social
scene: Chickens fleeing across a lawn in every direction, an old woman in a straw hat waving a broom, students diving after birds.
text: Forty chickens are loose on the main lawn, pursued by an old woman in a straw hat. "Don't just stand there, dearie!" she shouts at you. "Grab the speckled one, she's the ringleader!"
> left: Keep walking
  say: You hear a crash, a squawk and a triumphant cackle behind you. The chickens, it seems, are caught.
> right: Grab the speckled one
  meet maud
  check vigor 10:
    rel maud +8
    say: You tackle the ringleader. The rest give up. "Good hands," says Old Maud, pressing a warm egg into your palm. "Come for tea."
  else:
    rel maud +5
    health -2
    say: The ringleader escapes and pecks you, but Maud is impressed by your enthusiasm. "Come for tea. Bring plasters."

@event maud_honey
title: Honey for a Cold
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 5 and (has(sick) or health < 40)
weight: 18
art: flower
tags: nature
scene: A small cottage kitchen with bundles of herbs hanging from the beams, an old woman pouring golden honey into a steaming mug.
text: Maud spots you sniffling across the lawn and drags you into her cottage. "Sit," she orders, pouring honey into something steaming that smells of lemon and thunder.
> left: Drink it all
  health +12
  lose sick
  rel maud +4
  say: It tastes like summer and lightning. By morning you're cured and slightly glowing.
> right: Drink it and help with chores
  health +8
  lose sick
  rel maud +8
  alchemy +1
  say: You sip and sort herbs while she tells you the names of every plant in the room. You remember most of them.

@event maud_old_student
title: Maud Was a Student Once
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 15 and hollow >= 1
weight: 14
art: moon
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: An old woman sitting on a bench by the lake at dusk, looking at the water as if it might look back.
text: "I was a student here, you know," Maud says, watching the lake. "Sixty years ago. The lake froze one spring. Three of my friends went down to the boathouse that night. Only two came back." She doesn't look at you. "Ask me what I know."
> left: "You don't have to tell me."
  rel maud +6
  say: She pats your hand. "Kind. But time's short, dearie." She tells you anyway, a little at a time, over many cups of tea.
  hollow +1
> right: "What do you know?"
  rel maud +4
  hollow +1
  flag knows_founders_seal
  say: "Seven locks, one in each tower. The key's a star that eats light. And the thing below loves a lonely heart." She finally looks at you. "Don't be lonely."

@event maud_bees
title: The Silver Bees
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 10 and month >= 7 and month <= 10
weight: 10
art: flower
tags: nature
scene: Wooden hives in a wildflower meadow, an old woman in a veiled hat lifting a frame dripping with silver honey, bees glinting in the sun.
text: "The silver bees need moving to the summer meadow," Maud says, handing you a veiled hat. "They're friendly. Mostly. Don't make any sudden thoughts."
> left: Help with the hives
  check vigor 12:
    health +4
    rel maud +6
    gold +10
    say: The bees hum around you like a blessing. Maud gives you a jar of silver honey that sells for ten crowns. You eat half first.
  else:
    health -6
    rel maud +4
    say: You have a sudden thought. The bees know. You spend the evening with vinegar on your stings.
> right: Watch from a safe distance
  mood +3
  say: You watch Maud move hives barehanded, singing to them. It's the calmest you've felt all month.

@event maud_ill
title: Maud Is Unwell
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 20 and year >= 2 and not flag(maud_ill_done)
weight: 12
art: house
tags: social
scene: A small cottage bedroom with a patchwork quilt, an old woman propped up on pillows, a student reading aloud by candlelight.
text: Maud's chickens are running wild, unfed. You find her in bed, grey-faced and coughing. "Just a chill," she wheezes. "I'm eighty-one. I'm allowed."
> left: Fetch Sister Amaranth
  flag maud_ill_done
  rel maud +6
  say: Amaranth brings tonics and a stern lecture. Maud is back on her feet in a week, grumbling about fuss.
> right: Look after her yourself for a week
  flag maud_ill_done
  rel maud +14
  grades -3
  gain blessed
  say: You feed chickens, brew teas, read her the newspaper. When she's well, she gives you a sprig of rosemary. "You'll do," she says. "You'll do."

# ================= HEADMISTRESS ISOLDE MARROW =================

@event isolde_intro
title: She Knows Your Name
actor: isolde
when: not met(isolde) and turn >= 3
weight: 10
art: crown
tags: story
scene: A tall pale woman in dark robes pausing behind a student's chair in a candlelit dining hall, a hand resting lightly on the chair back.
text: At dinner, a cool hand rests on the back of your chair. The headmistress. "{player}," she says, though you've never met. "Your marks in Arcana are interesting. Your marks in punctuality, less so." She moves on.
> left: Stammer an apology
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +2
  say: She's already three tables away. Every student between you sits a little straighter.
> right: "Interesting how, Headmistress?"
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +4
  renown +2
  say: She pauses. Turns. Almost smiles. "Ask me again at the end of your first year," she says. The table stares at you.

@event isolde_tea
title: Tea in the Tower
trigger: social
actor: isolde
when: renown >= 25 and rel(isolde) >= 0
weight: 10
art: cup
tags: social
scene: A round tower study at twilight, two delicate teacups on a small table, a headmistress pouring tea with a perfectly steady hand.
text: An invitation to tea with the headmistress. Students talk about these the way soldiers talk about battles. She pours. "Tell me, {player}: what do you want to become?"
> left: Give an ambitious answer
  check charm 18:
    rel isolde +8
    renown +3
    say: She listens without interrupting, then says, "Good. Ambition without arrogance. Rarer than you'd think."
  else:
    rel isolde -2
    say: She nods politely. "Ambition is a fine servant," she says, "and a poor master." You're dismissed shortly after.
> right: Admit you don't know yet
  rel isolde +6
  lore +1
  say: "Neither did I, at your age," she says. "I still don't, some days. That's the point of an academy." She refills your cup.

@event isolde_warning
title: A Quiet Warning
trigger: social
actor: isolde
when: has(detention) or has(watched) or has(probation)
weight: 10
art: scales
tags: crisis
scene: A headmistress walking alongside a student in a long colonnade, hands clasped behind her back, speaking without looking at them.
text: The headmistress falls into step beside you in the colonnade. "I hear your name more often than I'd like," she says pleasantly. "In the wrong rooms. I'd hate to hear it in mine."
> left: Promise to do better
  rel isolde +3
  grades +3
  lose watched
  say: "Good." She stops walking. You keep going. When you look back, she's gone.
> right: Defend yourself
  check charm 20:
    rel isolde +5
    lose watched
    say: You lay it out plainly. She listens, then nods once. "Fair. I'll have a word with certain prefects."
  else:
    rel isolde -5
    say: "Hm," she says. "Let's hope you're right." It doesn't feel like hope.
